<p id="p2">It’s a big sports month for Apple TV, starting with Apple Arcade, which goes all-in on football with <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/madden-nfl-27-arcade-edition/id6755553408" rel="noopener noreferrer">Madden NFL 27 Arcade Edition</a> and <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/retro-bowl-college/id6745877228" rel="noopener noreferrer">Retro Bowl College+</a>. On the Apple TV side, <a href="https://www.apple.com/tv-pr/news/2026/04/apple-tvs-emmy-award-winning-global-smash-hit-series-ted-lasso-returns-for-season-four-on-wednesday-august-5/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ted Lasso</a> returns for a fourth season, Formula 1 is coming out of its summer break, the MLS Leagues Cup begins, and MLB continues.</p>
<p id="p3">Let’s take a closer look.</p>
<h2 id="apple-arcade">Apple Arcade</h2>
<p id="p4">Apple Arcade is adding two new games this month, both on Thursday, August 6, and both of them football games. That’s not a coincidence. The NFL and college football seasons are right around the corner, and these games offer great ways to get ready for both. They’re also part of a broader trend across Apple Arcade where sports games like <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/nba-2k25-arcade-edition/id6504000920" rel="noopener noreferrer">NBA 2K26</a> and <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pga-tour-pro-golf/id6545262709" rel="noopener noreferrer">PGA TOUR Pro Golf</a>, which also have continued receiving updates, have found a fan base.</p>
<h3 id="madden-nfl-27-arcade-edition-release-date-august-6"><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/madden-nfl-27-arcade-edition/id6755553408" rel="noopener noreferrer">Madden NFL 27 Arcade Edition</a> (Release Date: August 6)</h3>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/08/01/apple-arcade-madden-nfl-27-arcade-edition-2-1785617503497-43b92b656e.jpg" alt="Source: Apple."><p class="image-caption">Source: Apple.</p></div>
<p id="p6">The headliner this month is Madden NFL 27 Arcade Edition, an all-new entry in EA’s long-running NFL franchise built specifically for Apple Arcade. The game includes Franchise and Quick Play modes, featuring current NFL player rosters and ratings that adapt to real-world performance. And as part of Arcade, the game cane be played across iPhone, iPad, Mac, Apple TV, and Apple Vision Pro with controller support and no ads, paywalls, or in-app purchases.</p>
<p id="p7">I got a chance to play an early release version of Madden NFL 27, and it looks and plays great on Apple devices. I’m not the football fan I once was, but the Arcade game is excellent, capturing the excitement of game day whether you drop in for a Quick Play session or go deep, acting as the GM of a team. Madden NFL 27 is a terrific addition to the Apple Arcade lineup.</p>
